{
  "info": {
    "name": "CarbonLedger Pause API",
    "_postman_id": "c1f7a08b-6218-42f2-9599-73bf5e1564aa",
    "description": "# CarbonLedger Pause API\n\nCloses #1197\n\nThis collection covers all four pause-related endpoints for the CarbonLedger smart contract emergency circuit breaker.\n\n## Endpoints\n- **GET** `/api/v1/contract/status` — Current pause state (no auth)\n- **POST** `/api/v1/admin/pause` — Trigger emergency pause (admin)\n- **POST** `/api/v1/admin/unpause` — Lift active pause (admin)\n- **GET** `/api/v1/admin/pause-history` — Audit log of pause events (admin)\n\n## Setup\n1. Import `CarbonLedger_Testnet.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Set `adminAuthToken` to a valid admin JWT.\n3. Run requests in order (1 → 2 → 3 → 4) for a complete test cycle.\n\n## Authentication\nAdmin endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer {{adminAuthToken}}`.\n\nThe status endpoint is public — no authentication required.\n\n## Error codes\n- `EmergencyPaused` (29/27) — write blocked by active pause\n- `InvalidPauseWindow` (28/26) — `until_timestamp` out of valid range `(now, now+72h]`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "version": "2.0.0"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://api.carbonledger.io",
      "description": "CarbonLedger API base URL (override per environment)",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminAuthToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Admin JWT — set in your environment file",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "pauseDurationHours",
      "value": "2",
      "description": "Default pause duration in hours (1–72)",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "pauseReason",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically by pre-request script",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "lastPauseTxHash",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically after a successful pause",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "lastPauseUntil",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically after a successful pause",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Get Contract Status",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// No authentication required for this endpoint.",
              "// Clear any stale test variables from previous runs.",
              "pm.variables.set('statusCheckTime', new Date().toISOString());"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Response time under 2000ms', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(2000);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Response is valid JSON', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.be.json;",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Response has required fields', function () {",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('isPaused');",
              "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('status');",
              "    pm.expect(json.isPaused).to.be.a('boolean');",
              "    pm.expect(json.status).to.be.a('string');",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('status field has a valid value', function () {",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json.status).to.be.oneOf(['operational', 'paused', 'expiring_soon']);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('pauseUntil is null or a positive integer when paused', function () {",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    if (json.isPaused) {",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil).to.be.above(0);",
              "    } else {",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil === null || json.pauseUntil === undefined).to.be.true;",
              "    }",
              "});",
              "",
              "// Store current pause state for downstream tests",
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('contractIsPaused', json.isPaused);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('contractStatus', json.status);",
              "if (json.pauseUntil) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentPauseUntil', json.pauseUntil);",
              "}",
              "",
              "console.log('[Status check]', json.status,",
              "    json.isPaused ? `- paused until ${new Date(json.pauseUntil * 1000).toISOString()}` : '');",
              ""
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/contract/status",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "contract", "status"]
        },
        "description": "Retrieve the current operational status of the CarbonLedger contracts.\n\n**No authentication required.**\n\nReturns:\n- `isPaused` (bool) — whether the contract is currently blocking writes\n- `status` — `\"operational\"`, `\"paused\"`, or `\"expiring_soon\"`\n- `pauseUntil` — Unix timestamp when pause expires (null if not paused)\n- `reason` — human-readable reason for the pause (null if not paused)\n\nThe effective pause formula is:\n```\nis_effectively_paused = isPaused == true AND pauseUntil > current_time\n```\nEven if `isPaused` is `true`, the contract is not blocking writes once `pauseUntil` is in the past (stale flag)."
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK — Contract operational",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/contract/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "contract", "status"]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
            { "key": "X-Correlation-Id", "value": "req-abc123" }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"isPaused\": false,\n  \"status\": \"operational\",\n  \"pauseUntil\": null,\n  \"reason\": null,\n  \"contractVersion\": \"1.0.0\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "200 OK — Contract paused",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/contract/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "contract", "status"]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"isPaused\": true,\n  \"status\": \"paused\",\n  \"pauseUntil\": 1756486400,\n  \"reason\": \"Oracle price anomaly detected — investigation in progress\",\n  \"contractVersion\": \"1.0.0\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "200 OK — Pause expiring soon",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/contract/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "contract", "status"]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"isPaused\": true,\n  \"status\": \"expiring_soon\",\n  \"pauseUntil\": 1756480000,\n  \"reason\": \"Scheduled maintenance window\",\n  \"contractVersion\": \"1.0.0\"\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Emergency Pause Contract",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Validate admin token is set",
              "const token = pm.environment.get('adminAuthToken') || pm.collectionVariables.get('adminAuthToken');",
              "if (!token || token.trim() === '') {",
              "    throw new Error('adminAuthToken is not set. Update it in your environment file before running this request.');",
              "}",
              "",
              "// Build a timestamped reason so each run is distinct in the audit log",
              "const reason = `Postman automated test — emergency pause verification at ${new Date().toISOString()}`;",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('pauseReason', reason);",
              "",
              "// Default duration if not set",
              "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('pauseDurationHours')) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('pauseDurationHours', '2');",
              "}",
              "",
              "console.log('[Pre-request] Triggering pause with reason:', reason);"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Pause succeeds (200) or contract already paused (409)', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 409]);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Response is valid JSON', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.be.json;",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    pm.test('Success response has required fields', function () {",
              "        const json = pm.response.json();",
              "        pm.expect(json).to.have.property('success');",
              "        pm.expect(json).to.have.property('transactionHash');",
              "        pm.expect(json).to.have.property('pauseUntil');",
              "        pm.expect(json).to.have.property('affectedContracts');",
              "        pm.expect(json.success).to.equal(true);",
              "        pm.expect(json.transactionHash).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil).to.be.a('number').and.above(0);",
              "        pm.expect(Array.isArray(json.affectedContracts)).to.be.true;",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    pm.test('pauseUntil is in the future', function () {",
              "        const json = pm.response.json();",
              "        const nowSeconds = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil).to.be.above(nowSeconds);",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    pm.test('pauseUntil is within 72 hours', function () {",
              "        const json = pm.response.json();",
              "        const nowSeconds = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
              "        const maxAllowed = nowSeconds + (72 * 3600);",
              "        pm.expect(json.pauseUntil).to.be.at.most(maxAllowed);",
              "    });",
              "",
              "    // Store for use in unpause test",
              "    const json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('lastPauseTxHash', json.transactionHash);",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('lastPauseUntil', json.pauseUntil);",
              "    console.log('[Pause] TX:', json.transactionHash,",
              "        '| Until:', new Date(json.pauseUntil * 1000).toISOString());",
              "} else if (pm.response.code === 409) {",
              "    pm.test('409 body indicates already-paused state', function () {",
              "        const json = pm.response.json();",
              "        pm.expect(json).to.have.property('error');",
              "    });",
              "    console.warn('[Pause] Contract already paused — skipping. Check contract status first.');",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{adminAuthToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"durationHours\": {{pauseDurationHours}},\n  \"reason\": \"{{pauseReason}}\",\n  \"affectedContracts\": [\"carbon_credit\", \"carbon_marketplace\"]\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pause",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pause"]
        },
        "description": "Trigger an emergency pause across the specified CarbonLedger contracts.\n\n**Requires:** Admin JWT in `Authorization: Bearer` header.\n\n**Request body fields:**\n- `durationHours` (required, 1–72) — how long the pause should last\n- `reason` (required) — human-readable explanation, stored in the audit log\n- `affectedContracts` (optional) — which contracts to pause; defaults to both\n\n**Response codes:**\n- `200` — pause activated successfully\n- `400` — `durationHours` is out of range or missing\n- `403` — caller is not an admin\n- `409` — contract is already paused\n\nAfter a successful pause, all write operations on the affected contracts return `409 Conflict` with error code `EmergencyPaused` until the pause expires or is lifted via the unpause endpoint."
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK — Pause activated",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pause",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pause"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"durationHours\": 2,\n  \"reason\": \"Oracle price anomaly\",\n  \"affectedContracts\": [\"carbon_credit\", \"carbon_marketplace\"]\n}"
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"transactionHash\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f67890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890\",\n  \"pauseUntil\": 1756486400,\n  \"affectedContracts\": [\"carbon_credit\", \"carbon_marketplace\"],\n  \"initiatedBy\": \"GADMIN7J2XNQ5B6E4Y8WZ3M1K9L0P5R7T2V4X6Z8A0BADMIN\"\n}"
        },
        {
